=== PART 2. DECISION 1 -- WHICH GRADIENT IS THE TARGET? ===
Handoff sec.4.4 quotes +244.7 umol/kg and -0.938 permil. The SHIPPED
data/obs_glodap_deep.rds gives +233.1 and -0.861. BOTH ARE IN THE REPO and
they are not the same target. The difference is the layer definition, and
it is ~1 sigma on both fields -- so this is decision 1's actual content.

layer definition                                              DIC grad   d13C grad
shipped rds (0-100 / 2627.2-Inf, <=)                           +233.11     -0.8610
model boxes at h_ml = 50    (0-50 / 2620-3700, <)              +252.12     -0.9754
model boxes at h_ml = 75    (0-75 / 2627-3700, <) <- default h_ml, = handoff sec.4.4     +244.71     -0.9380
model boxes at h_ml = 100   (0-100 / 2635-3700, <) <- h_ml under the pump (15d)     +234.98     -0.8852
model boxes at h_ml = 140   (0-140 / 2646-3700, <)             +224.53     -0.8156
model boxes at h_ml = 184   (0-184 / 2659-3700, <) <- FITTED h_ml (clause 1)     +212.79     -0.7472
model boxes at h_ml = 220   (0-220 / 2670-3700, <)             +203.66     -0.6953

THE MODEL-ANCHORED TARGET IS A FUNCTION OF h_ml: +212.8 umol/kg at
h_ml = 184 and +235.0 at h_ml = 100 -- it moves +22.2 umol/kg as h_ml
falls 184 -> 100, which is the exact move the pump makes (15d).

So an h_ml-anchored target is a FUNCTION OF A FITTED PARAMETER, and the
term would be partly scoring its own layer choice. Part 2b prices BOTH
ways out, because neither is neutral and their biases point OPPOSITE ways.


=== PART 2b. THE TWO WAYS OUT, PRICED -- AND THEIR BIASES POINT OPPOSITE WAYS ===
Frozen-at-h_ml-75 target: +244.71 umol/kg. Priced against sigma_Delta
from part 3 (tightest valid block), which is why this table prints AFTER it.


=== PART 3. DECISION 2 -- SIGMA ON THE GRADIENT, MEASURED ===
Estimand Delta = xbar_deep - xbar_surf, so Var(Delta) = Var(D) + Var(S)
- 2 Cov(D,S) and the covariance is measured, not assumed. Layers are the
SHIPPED rds ones so this sigma pairs with the shipped target; part 2's
other definitions change the CENTRE far more than they change the spread.


