ALL THREE DEEP LEVELS LAND IN THE SAME BRACKET, ~10 to ~26, and
LIK_D14C_DEEP_NEFF = 20 sits inside it for every field. So sec.4.6's
worry does NOT bite for the LEVEL formulation: DIC and d13C do have their
own spatial structure, and it does not move n_eff enough to matter.
IT DOES BITE FOR THE GRADIENT, for the reason in part 3b -- the contrast
has a different and larger sampling error than either level.


=== PART 4. THE CONSTANT THE TERMS ADD ===
Handoff sec.4.2 puts it at ~384 log-units from LEVEL terms with deep DIC
1996.2555 and deep d13C 1.55953. The model is recomputed here rather than
copied, because a constant quoted from a stale spinup is exactly the class
of number this repo has been bitten by.

hemi       DIC surf     DIC deep     DIC grad    d13C deep    d13C grad
NH        1986.3340    1986.3340     4.55e-13      1.55953     8.88e-13
SH        2003.7207    2003.7207     0.00e+00      1.55953     1.11e-12

THE MODEL'S INTERIOR IS UNIFORM TO MACHINE PRECISION, which is handoff
sec.4.2's zero-leverage result restated: the gradient IS the miss, in full.

term                                         miss      sigma          z  log-units
DIC gradient (shipped layers)            -233.109    19.8196     -11.76       69.2  (tightest valid block)
DIC gradient (shipped layers)            -233.109    25.2736      -9.22       42.5  (loosest valid block)
d13C gradient (shipped layers)              0.861     0.0747      11.53       66.5  (tightest valid block)
d13C gradient (shipped layers)              0.861     0.1148       7.50       28.1  (loosest valid block)

TOTAL CONSTANT ADDED BY THE TWO GRADIENT TERMS: 71 to 136 log-units
(handoff sec.4.2's LEVEL formulation gave ~384; these are GRADIENT terms
on the shipped layers, which is the sec.4.3 recommendation for d13C.)

This is a CONSTANT only while the model's interior is uniform. The pump
breaks that on purpose -- which is the point of adding the terms, and the
reason handoff sec.4.2 asks for a test asserting zero leverage with the
pump OFF so the day it stops holding is visible.


